    "explanation": "The driver filed this dispute asking for the 1.30 SGD that was refunded to the rider on 2026-09-14 at 20:14:30 and recovered from his earnings. The 1.30 SGD stays with the rider and the driver's claim fails, so the present state stands.\n\nMeasuring the deviation (POL-RD-22): the platform's recorded distances are 11.6 km actual against 9.8 km optimal, a deviation of 1.80 km. The 1.0 km tolerance is exceeded, and the clause does not allow the sparse GPS trace (9.795 km) to be used to re-measure it.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23): the only traffic data in the record is LTA-TI-260914-6951 (EV-ADVIS-05020-01), a ROAD_CLOSURE on Bukit Timah Road between Farrer Road and Cluny Road valid 00:30-05:30. The trip ran 18:34:30 to 19:00:30, so the advisory's window closed about thirteen hours before the journey; its own derived finding records overlaps_trip_window = false and justifies_reroute = false. The driver's in-app message of 18:41:22 ('Bukit Timah Road got road closure, I go Holland Road ok?') is an assertion of traffic and, under POL-RD-23, an assertion with no qualifying data does not justify the reroute. The rider's statement that the road was open and moving is consistent with the data.\n\nApplying the matrix (POL-RD-24): because the reroute was not traffic-justified and the deviation is over 1 km, row (d) applies and the excess distance fare is refunded in full. That fare is 1.80 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.296, rounded to 1.30 SGD, with no surge. This is exactly the sum the ledger shows as refund_issued_sgd 1.30 (EV-FARE-05020, payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED) and the fare_adjusted event shows was refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver. The rider is therefore owed the 1.30 SGD, and under POL-GEN-03 the filing driver's claim is not supported: the outcome is NO_ACTION with both amounts null, and the rider keeps the money.\n\nThe driver's points are answered. His claim that he told the rider before deviating and she replied 'ok sure' (POL-RD-21) is accepted on the chat log — MSG-05020-003 at 18:41:22 was read at 18:41:33, the rider answered at 18:41:47, and the platform's deviation event is at 18:44:22 — but that only reaches row (a) if the reroute was also traffic-justified, and it was not; rows (b) and (d) refund the same 1.30 SGD whether or not the rider was informed, so the point does not change the outcome. His point that the advisory names the very road and the diversion he took is noted but does not satisfy POL-RD-23, whose test is overlap with the trip window, and he concedes that limb is not met. His request in the alternative for escalation under POL-RD-24's 'fits no row' limb is rejected: this case fits row (d) squarely, so the escalation limb is not engaged, and the fact that the rider now says her agreement rested on the driver's closure claim goes to the premise of a message she accepted, not to any element row (d) requires.\n\nConfidence and forum: the deciding facts are carried by complete artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-TRIP-05020, EV-GPS-05020, EV-FARE-05020, EV-ADVIS-05020-01), so the cap is 1.0. POL-GEN-22 places the contested 1.30 SGD below 10.00 SGD, where the AI ruling is final at any confidence, and POL-RD-25's 0.80 bar is met. Route deviation produces no referral, so none is made.",
